gas: pin the obstack chunk size for cross-host reproducible builds

gas leaves its global `chunksize` at 0, which tells the obstack library to
pick its own default chunk size, computed as `4096 - extra`.  That "extra"
term is computed differently by glibc's obstack (used when gas is built on
Linux) and libiberty's obstack (used on Darwin and other hosts whose libc
lacks obstack), so the effective frag-obstack chunk size depends on which
libc gas was linked against.

`frag_grow` (gas/frags.c) closes the current frag and starts a new one when
the current obstack chunk runs out of room.  Because the chunk size differs
per host, these chunk-exhaustion splits land at different byte offsets, which
flips `frag == last_frag` in dwarf2dbg.c:process_entries, which flips the
`.debug_line` encoding between an absolute DW_LNE_set_address (+ relocation)
and a relative PC advance.  The result: the same assembly input produces
byte-different `.o` files on different build hosts (verified: a gnumach i686
kernel built on aarch64-darwin vs aarch64-linux/x86_64 diverged in
`.debug_line` for a handful of translation units; the divergence disappears
once the chunk size is pinned).

Pinning `chunksize` to a fixed value makes the chunk size - and therefore the
split points and the emitted `.debug_line` - identical regardless of the
obstack implementation, without otherwise changing gas's behaviour (4096 is
the same size the zero-default already targets).

This is a local reproducibility fix; it has not (yet) been submitted upstream.

diff --git a/gas/as.c b/gas/as.c
index 449167d..eeb996a 100644
--- a/gas/as.c
+++ b/gas/as.c
@@ -88,7 +88,16 @@ static char * myname;

 /* The default obstack chunk size.  If we set this to zero, the
    obstack code will use whatever will fit in a 4096 byte block.  */
-int chunksize = 0;
+/* ...but that zero-default is computed inside the obstack library as
+   (4096 - extra), and "extra" differs between glibc's obstack and
+   libiberty's obstack.  The resulting chunk size therefore depends on
+   which libc gas is linked against, which moves frag_grow's
+   chunk-exhaustion split points, which in turn perturbs the .debug_line
+   program (DW_LNE_set_address vs a relative advance) for the same input.
+   That makes object files non-reproducible across build hosts.  Pin the
+   chunk size to a fixed value so split points are identical regardless of
+   the obstack implementation.  */
+int chunksize = 4096;

 /* To monitor memory allocation more effectively, make this non-zero.
    Then the chunk sizes for gas and bfd will be reduced.  */
